\documentclass{article}
\title{Spatio-Temporal Modeling for Traffic Forecasting}
\author{S. Park}
\begin{document}
\maketitle
\section{Introduction}
Traffic forecasting is a core component of ITS. Recent work applies GNN to capture spatial dependencies between sensors, while RNN and its variants model temporal dynamics. We propose a model that combines both ideas: the GNN module learns the sensor graph directly from data, and the temporal module replaces the vanilla RNN with a gated design.
\section{Experiments}
We evaluate on two highway datasets with standard splits.
\end{document}
